    <name>HR Source import (full, development config)</name>
    <description>Experiment. Tests whether a resource in lifecycle state "proposed" prevents real execution, or only hides configuration from production-scoped tasks.</description>
    <documentation>This is an experiment, not an operational task.

Question: does a resource in lifecycle state `proposed` act as an execution barrier in its own right, or does it only hide the configuration from tasks running with production configuration scope?

Method: run an import in Full mode, with "Configuration to use" set to Development, against the HR Source (CSV) resource while it remains in `proposed`.

Both outcomes are acceptable, which is why the experiment is safe to run:

- Nothing is created. Then `proposed` is an execution barrier of its own, and the two protections are independent.
- Sixteen users are created. Then `proposed` only scopes which configuration is visible, and the safety in the earlier run came entirely from the task's own execution mode.

The sixteen users are going to be created in any case, so the second outcome costs nothing.</documentation>
